    "notes": "A title open (the warehouse, then Rigg's look under our RIGG title and glint, over the Lyria theme), the premise (our 00:30 digits on a plain-faced device still, he shoulders the door and it doesn't move), a fast montage on the lock, the hinge and the frame cut against our countdown at 00:19, 00:09, 00:03 and 00:02 under a rising tension cue, the climax line and the spray can taped to the hinge. The music cuts dead on the 00:02 beep; the door swings in toward him, pulled from outside, she is standing there with two coffees, a beat, \"Rigg. It's a pull.\", he turns to the camera, freeze and the theme as a sting. Ported from rigg5/edit.mjs. Every Rigg line is from one continuous take (rigg5-lines-t2 as extended by rigg5-climax-t1); \"Need a tension wrench.\" and \"Hinge pins. Painted shut.\" are laid from it over the lock and hinge inserts as L-cuts, each a line carrying its own stretch of that take. Each countdown shot is the device still held, our digits drawn into it, pushing in 5% to its end, with its beep (a 1950 Hz tone for 0.11 s) as its own sound. The tension cue is placed by its sync point: its first big hit, 7.45 s into the file, lands on the first montage cut. The whole mix runs through a limiter at 0.95."
  },
